 "comment": "WP-2.G, Gate 2's headless scripted session (PLAN_v4 §5 Gate 2: generate a world, walk, dig, place, craft, fight, sleep, save, reload). Seed 123 generated terrain, difficulty 1, natural spawning off, saved through SaveOldDir. The player (id 0) starts on the grass at (-25.5, 67, -57.5) (surface y = 66 there, checked with a block_box probe) facing +z (yaw 0) with a stone shovel, stone pickaxe, stone sword, 2 logs, a bed, 10 dirt and a bread in hotbar slots 0-6. Walk: forward for 60 ticks (t=1-60, downhill to about z = -45.4, feet at y = 64), then stop. Dig: the grass block in front of the feet, (-26,63,-45), with the shovel (t=62-69; broken at t=67 on the held repeat click); then forward again from t=70 into the hole, where the dropped dirt is picked up (11 dirt). Place: dirt on top of (-24,63,-44) with use_item (ItemBlock.onItemUse, WP-2.6). Craft: in the player's 2x2 grid by slot_click (container slots: 0 output, 1-4 grid, 9-35 main, 36-44 hotbar): both logs into the grid, two clicks on the output (8 planks), two planks in a column (4 sticks, put into main slot 10, the other 6 planks into slot 9), four planks (a crafting table, into hotbar slot 7), then three craft ops (log, two planks in a column, four planks) as recipe checks; the crafting table placed on (-24,63,-43). Fight: a zombie (id 1) is spawned at t=0 on the grass at (-66.5, 68, -57.5), 41 blocks west of the player and out of its 16-block target range, so its id does not depend on the terrain (population constructs no entity; the falling sand of the first ticks takes the ids after it), which keeps the scenario runnable under check-sensitivity.sh's flipped seed (for the same reason a fill with air clears its spawn spot and its destination: no-ops here, changed 0, but in other terrain they keep it from suffocating before the fight); it wanders and burns in daylight until t=110, when set_pos puts it 6 blocks from the player at (-25.5, 64, -38.5) (set_motion 0). It walks towards the hole; three sword attacks 12 ticks apart (t=150, 162, 174) kill it; its drop roll (Item.feather, rand.nextInt(3)) and the 20-tick death follow. Then the bread is eaten (use_item on a block: ItemFood.onItemRightClick through sendUseItem). Sleep: world time set to 18000, the bed placed on (-24,63,-48) with use_item (ItemBed.onItemUse: foot at (-24,64,-48), head at +z), the sleep op on the foot (status OK); after 100 ticks World.tick finds every player fully asleep, sets the time to the next morning (24000) and wakes the player at the bed (spawn point set), so no set_time to morning is needed. Save (t=310: Tier S lines for the walk's start chunk (-2,-4) and the player's chunk (-2,-3), which holds every edit), then the reload op: the world saved, dropped and opened again, its 429 chunks loaded again, the player read from level.dat with a new id (2045; the saved item entities come back with new ids too; the hotbar selection, not saved, is slot 0 again). 100 more ticks and a final save at t=410. Dumps: rng_state and the player's entity line every tick, player_state every 10, inventory, every entity, world time and the 3x3 chunks around chunk (-2,-3) every 20, the edited blocks at fixed ticks.",
